                    <msContents>
                        <summary>Donation of gold, including Chinese gold (<foreign>cinakkanakam</foreign>) by an officer (<foreign>kaṉmi</foreign>) of the king of Kiṭāram, named Agralēkai alias Kuruttaṉ Kēcuvaṉ, for offering rituals (<foreign>avipali arccaṉai</foreign>) to the Ardhanāri that he had installed in the Tirukkārōṇam temple in Nākapaṭṭiṉam.</summary>
                    </msContents>
